I ruled on pool-closing-1 and took option A, the one the operator recommended. It is a clarification only and does not change any contract. I skipped the optional Jev citation check.

`expectNoA11yViolations` needs a Playwright page, so it cannot run in a Vitest component test. `src/lib/fzp/MoneyResults.svelte.spec.ts` now runs axe-core directly instead:
- It checks the rendered money block with the same WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2 A and AA tags that `expectNoA11yViolations` uses.
- It runs once in light and once in dark, switching the colour scheme the way `MapKeyControl.svelte.spec.ts` does.
- It expects no violations.

The "ran out" lines are plain text, not controls, so the rule that every new control passes the a11y check doesn't call for an e2e test. pool-closing's write set stays as it was.

The only file I changed is the pool-closing spec (§ sec-tests-money), committed as "docs(incremental-game): rule pool-closing-1". pool-closing is the only affected unit, and it only needs a clarification. Its plan stands.

